UT: [C002 invariant] a restoration failure is never passed over silently — the invariant predicate
```js
// C002 invariant: a locked worktree cannot be destroyed, and that is blocking.
await assert.rejects(
  () => withIsolatedWorktree(root, async (worktreePath) => {
    // A real lock makes `git worktree remove --force` fail, exactly as a real
    // restoration failure would; nothing about git is simulated here.
    runGit(root, ['worktree', 'lock', worktreePath]);
    return { redProved: true };
  }),
  (error) => error.name === 'WorktreeIsolationError'
    && error.reason === 'restoration-failed'
    && error.outcome.restorationOutcome === 'failed'
    && error.outcome.mainTreeDigest.unchanged === true
    && error.outcome.worktreePath !== null,
);

// The failure is not swallowed even when the reconstruction itself also threw:
// the restoration failure leads, and the execution error is preserved as cause.
await assert.rejects(
  () => withIsolatedWorktree(root, async (worktreePath) => {
    runGit(root, ['worktree', 'lock', worktreePath]);
    throw new Error('the reconstruction failed partway');
  }),
  (error) => error.reason === 'restoration-failed'
    && error.cause?.message === 'the reconstruction failed partway',
);
```

